Z||000006||FieroLT1||06-08-2001||10:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B>Thanks guys....<BR>Winston, I actually did a search for "Fiero LT1" yesterday looking for more info, and gyess who's site popped up?! <BR>If you have any accelleration times with an LT1 on a 5sp getrag on street tires (specifically 0-60) I would be very interested. Someone in another thread said around 4.1 sec, and someone else called it "hype". <BR>Thanks!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, I monitored that thread very carefully and was not in the mood of starting anything. But the guy that said that, it's clear that has never riden an LT1 powered Fiero. Granted the 4.1s was taken with a stop watch in hand, but I still think is it a conservative number. I am in the process of getting a G-tech Pro. When I get, it I'll reconfirm that and other times and make sure I'll post it here.<BR>Yeap, It is a Hype alright!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
