Z||000009||Slammed Fiero||06-09-2001||03:54 PM||||I said hype based on several things. First and foremost having seen several people run 300hp Lt1's to low 13's in the 1/4. We have had a 383 LT1 lunati stroker 93 40th anniversary vette. It would pull mid 4's with about 100hp over stock and 120ft lbs over stock. The vette weighed in at 3275. Currently we have an 87.5 World challenge car (rare) with a built 355 small block.It's tuned a little more radically than the 93 was and weighs in about 100lbs less. The gear ratio's in both vettes were close ratio as in comparison to the Fiero's Getrag.<P>Both cars are mid 12 sec cars with 3.23 rear gears. The 87 Runs the Doug Nash 4+3 with the cags skip shift eliminator. The 93 was a borg warner t-56. Both cars were built for BSP autocross use. Low 13's in the 1/4 does not compute right with 4.1 to sixty. Considering a viper has 450hp and is usually pulling mid to low 4's and 12.2's-12.6's in the 1/4.<P>Our current dedicated autocross track car is a 94 911 RSR , 3.8ltr 367 Rear wheel hp , it's good for low 12's and 3.9 ro 60. Redlines at 8 grand, B&B triflow exhaust headers , champion motorsports built motor , TWM induction (1 tb per cylinder ..looks a lot like webbers) Plus the car weighs 2697. Whats a Lt1 Fiero weigh in at ?? 2950?<P>I don't doubt the car is very Fast with an LT1 , I have had lots of experience with Lt1's , as many people know we run an LT1 with LT4 heads on our Impala SS wagon.<BR>The numbers just don't compute<P>I just think 4.1 sec is pushing<BR>the envlope a bit with a warmed over LT1. I would believe high 4's low 5's.  Northstars in Fiero's run around the 5 sec flat mark. This done WITH a Gtec<P>I hopeno one takes this as an insult to their V8 Fiero ,it'snot meant to be at all.<P>And if you do muster a 4.1 sec to 60 ,more power to you.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
